>2). I can play the first 4 levels quite well, but
>every time I get to level 5 a killer bee gets me.
>What is the best way to fight a killer bee?

The best way to fight a killer bee at this stage is not to fight
a killer bee.

Nethack is tough to get a grasp on because it seems to be the 
equivalent of a 1st person shooter on the surface. See goblin,
kill goblin. See fox, kill fox. And the like.

But nethack is really a managment game with the ultimate goal
of managing to stay alive long enough to win the game.

By the way you've already figured out the most potent weapon
in a managment game: information. That's the tool you need
both in game and out of game to manage the situation. So I would
advise that you spoil yourself and read up.

The game is designed to counterbalance your actions. In general
this means that it punishes you when you attempt to tip things
too far into your favor.

You've listed two examples above. Teleportitis can be useful.
However you get some penalties for getting it and it makes
the game tough if you cannot manage it.

Killer bees comes in response to two actions: 1) going too deep
into the dungeon and 2) Having too much experience (called levelling
up in Nethack speak).

So like the old joke "Doctor, it hurts when I do this!" 
"Well, don't do that!"

Don't tackle killer bees until you can handle them. They sting.
They poison. They are hard to kill. And frankly killing them
gives you more experience, which levels you up more, which brings
even tougher monsters into the game.

Now let's talk about some positive things that you can do while you
are managing the early game.

1) You pet is your best friend and protector. They have lots of
admiriable qualities: fast, grow into ferocious defenders. But to
do that you need to let them kill monsters and eat most of them. 
Also I don't think they can bo poisoned. A buffed up pet would have
no problem taking out bees. The only thing to watch out for is the
fact that pets will stop everything to eat. Do if you have multiple
monsters attacking you'll have to manage that.

2) Work on your AC. Armor can save your butt. Another great pet
feature is that they'll tell you when armor is bad to put on
(i.e. drop and let them sniff it. If they pick it up or step on
it, then it's OK to wield/wear)

3) Understand the power of prayer in Nethack. A nethack character in
the good graces of their god can get many many benefits. Take a read
of the praying spoiler here:

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html

Take careful note of restored/added HP along with relieving hunger.

4) Shops. Lots of stuff. Lots of money. Take some time to clean them
out. Refer to point #1 and take a read of this spoiler:

http://www.helsinki.fi/~vviitane/spoilers/pets

Also if you want to get into a nethack gray area, take a read of a
couple of my previous posts about credit cloning in google groups.

5) One of the most satisfying early game goals is the protection
racket. I call it weight free crystal plate mail. You can read all
about it in the Pacifist FAQ here:

http://home.nycap.rr.com/rduhan/steves/pacfaq02.html

I use it as an early game strategy. Almost all of the techniques
outlined above are from that FAQ in one form or another.

All of this gets you prepared for midgame. Then bees will be an
annoyance to you and your pet because they can't hit you, you can 
whack them, and your pet will dispatch them in a single chomp.

Hope this gives you some insight.

